## Fee Clarification: Exit Load
### Reusable Support Snippet

  • Exit load is a charge applied only when units are redeemed before the fund’s specified minimum holding period; it is not levied on every redemption after that period.
  • The applicable percentage varies by scheme type (e.g., equity, debt, hybrid) and is disclosed in the scheme’s offer document; it is not a uniform rate across all categories.
  • The load is calculated on the gross redemption value (principal plus any accrued gains) and therefore reduces the amount received, not just the profit.
  • The load is not a hidden fee; it is disclosed in the scheme information memorandum and on transaction statements at the time of purchase and redemption.
  • For systematic investment plans (SIPs), each installment creates a separate holding period, so an early redemption of a particular installment may attract an exit load even if earlier installments have satisfied the minimum period.
  • GST at the prevailing rate is applicable on the exit load amount, and the tax is added to the load before deduction from the redemption proceeds.

**Official Sources:**
  - https://www.sebi.gov.in/legal/circulars/jun-2009/exit-load-mutual-funds_3555.html
  - https://www.amfiindia.com/investor-corner/knowledge-center/exit-load

